  "evidence": [
    "Pinned4C5780/4C5980 contain shared-base vtable reset, load/test provider at+14 and tail-dispatch slot4; current real derived destructors jump to an out-of-line base destructor. Pinned Wave_Device4C4E60 embeds the same base stage after reverse member-group destruction. This supports shared inline visibility, not changing hierarchy or hand-coding vtables.",
    "Move the unchanged protected nonvirtual SoundDeviceBase destructor definition from sounddevice.cpp to an ordinary inline definition in sounddevice.h, with the existing SoundX ABI include. Retain all derived destructor bodies, constructors, class layout, public declarations, mapped spans and claims. No forced export, retention wrapper, explicit vptr or new provider-class hypothesis.",
    "Wave_Device is a third derived class in a separate TU; a CPP-only inline trial is not a complete cross-TU definition. Review all three derived destructor symbols and global lifetime callbacks. Existing shared-base teardown after group destruction must remain intact, including exception paths.",
    "Three existing tests extract the old out-of-line body; update only source extraction and adjacent constructor bound, preserving runtime scenarios and mutation controls. Any new test file or outside-owner change needs explicit scope expansion.",
    "Header affects at least12 direct includers (graphicwin,net_class,popmenu,scroll,sound,sound_loader,sounddevice,spritebox,voice,wave,wave_device,win); compile full application and measure full source or proven closure. Verify emitted standalone identities, references, historical claim continuity and physical collateral. Missing emitted symbols or regressions are obligations, not silently accepted. Manual integration requires coordinator review; no game acceptance is implied."
  ],
  "intent": "Restore visibility of the real shared base-destructor body to all three concrete sound-device destructor owners.",
